          "status": "permitted"
        },
        {
          "id": "light-timber-frame-forbidden-in-family-cascade",
          "status": "canonical",
          "note": "The inherited Beaux-Arts/Baroque family rule states 'light timber frame construction has no place anywhere in this family.' The style's own description directly contradicts this: the colossal portico is 'a screen in front of a conventional balloon-framed or brick-bearing house.' That is the whole point of the style's honesty about its own thinness -- overridden here."
        }
      ],
      "rule": "The portico is very rarely doing structural work; it screens a conventional balloon-framed or brick-bearing house. Reverses the inherited Beaux-Arts-French rule that forbids light frame construction outright.",
      "status": "drafted"
