          "status": "permitted",
          "op": "add",
          "note": "defining_characteristics: columns rise 'to a pediment or entablature' -- the portico may terminate flat rather than in a pediment, an alternative the inherited Beaux-Arts American triangular/segmental pediment binding does not offer."
        }
      ],
      "status": "drafted"
    },
    "pilaster": {
      "group": "classical-apparatus",
      "binding": "specified",
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "pilaster-continuing-order-across-flanking-wall",
          "status": "permitted",
          "note": "Where used at all, a pilaster simply continues the portico's giant order across the plain flanking wall -- not the inherited Beaux-Arts-American system of paired pilasters filling a recessed wall between advanced pavilions, which presumes the pavilion massing this style does not use."
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {},
